commit 78fc633dbf6f9e1303157a16fac7826a26e43a01
Author:     Evan <suzukaze.haduki@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Aug 25 07:56:36 2026 +0900
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Mon Aug 24 22:56:36 2026 +0000

    chore(deps): upgrade rmcp to 3.1 and pin the client calls to the single-round helpers (#7885)
    
    rmcp 3.1 adds an inherent `impl<S> RunningService<RoleClient, S>` block that shadows two methods LibreFang previously reached through `Deref<Target = Peer<RoleClient>>`.
    The inherent `call_tool` and `read_resource` are MRTR drivers: they loop up to `DEFAULT_MRTR_MAX_ROUNDS` (10) SEP-2322 `input_required` rounds, and they capture `S` in the returned future.
    
    Both consequences are unwanted here.
    The loop would have run inside the existing `tokio::time::timeout`, so a budget written for one request would have silently covered ten.
    The captured `S` is what an inherent `async fn` leaks to the caller, and it made every future holding an `McpConnection` non-`Send`, which surfaced as 36 `Send is not general enough` errors in `librefang-kernel` — `cron_tick`, `inbox`, `goal_lifecycle`, `agent_control`, `approval_gate` and the workflow engine.
    Each of the two call sites reproduces all 36 on its own, so both had to move.
    
    `call_tool_once` / `read_resource_once` send exactly one request and are `Send`-clean.
    They are also the semantically faithful choice: `RootsClientHandler` advertises only `roots` in `ClientCapabilities`, declaring neither the tasks extension nor elicitation, so a compliant server has no license to send `input_required` or a task response.
    The non-`Complete` arms therefore return an error rather than silently dropping a response we never asked for.
    
    `ProtocolVersion::LATEST` is `2025-11-25` in both 2.2.0 and 3.1.4, so nothing changes on the wire.
    
    Verification:
    - `cargo check -p librefang-runtime-mcp --lib` and `--tests`: 0 errors.
    - `cargo check -p librefang-runtime --lib`, `cargo check -p librefang-kernel --lib`: 0 errors.
    - Baseline control on unmodified origin/main: `cargo check -p librefang-kernel --lib` is also 0, confirming the 36 errors were attributable to the bump and not to a pre-existing break.
    - `cargo fmt --check -p librefang-runtime-mcp`.
    
    Refs #6749

